course: dictionary
lesson: 15312
title: Sluggish: slow and without energy
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «After the big Sunday lunch, Dad felt sluggish and fell asleep on the sofa.» The clues are the big lunch and falling asleep. Sluggish means slow and tired, with no energy.
explain: Sluggish can also describe machines. «The old tablet was so sluggish that every app took minutes to open.» A sluggish tablet is slow to respond. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: "so slow to respond that every app took minutes" still makes sense.
explain: Sluggish can describe water and money too. «The river was sluggish in the summer heat, barely moving across the flat fields.» Here it means flowing slowly. Read the words around sluggish first, and they will tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Sluggish is an adjective, and its adverb is sluggishly.
fact: «Sluggish» means moving or working slowly, without much energy.
fact: «Sluggish» can also mean slow to respond, as in a sluggish computer.
fact: «Sluggish» can describe a slow river, or trade and money that are not growing much.
fact: Cold-blooded animals like lizards can be sluggish when it is cold.
exercise: «After the big meal, Sam felt sluggish and wanted to nap.» What does sluggish mean here? | *Slow and tired, without energy | Lost and confused | Very angry | Full of bounce and fast
exercise: «The old tablet was so sluggish that each app took minutes to open.» What does sluggish suggest about the tablet? | *Slow to respond | Very bright and colourful | Brand new | Waterproof
exercise: «The river flowed sluggishly across the flat plain.» What does sluggishly mean? | Sadly | Up and down | *Slowly | Quickly and loudly
test: «Trade was sluggish this year, so shops sold fewer goods.» What does sluggish mean here? | *Not growing much; slow | Very noisy | Cold and wet | Full of energy
test: «The lizard was sluggish in the cold morning air.» Why might the lizard be sluggish? | It is wearing a warm coat | It has just won a race | It is very hungry and fast | *Its body is cold, so it moves slowly
exam: «After a sleepless night, Mia's sluggish reactions made her miss the ball.» What does sluggish mean here? | Very fast and sharp | Brand new | Happy and loud | *Slow to react, because she is tired
